# === Machine-specific settings (see .env.example) ===
/.env

# === Python / uv ===
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# === VIBE ===
.agents
.claude
skills-lock.json

# === Local research workspace: literature notes, agent findings and
# downloaded papers/patents (personal working copies, not redistributed).
# Anchored to repo root. ===
/research/

# === OS / IDE ===
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
*.code-workspace

# === Windows shell-redirection artifact (some agent tooling creates a literal
# 'nul' file instead of redirecting to the NUL device) ===
nul
**/nul

# === Extraction/pipeline outputs ===
data/extracted/

# === Remotely-uploaded IFC files (vite.config.js's /api/upload-ifc) - each
# upload gets its own data/uploads/<uploadId>/ folder (raw .ifc + its
# extraction cache), isolated from other uploads and from the data/*.ifc
# dev fixtures below. Same confidentiality/large-file reasoning as the "Raw
# IFC test data" rule right after this one. ===
data/uploads/

# === Raw IFC models (large, and most are not ours to publish). Mirrors the
# existing *.ifc rule in Interfaces/Frontend/data_vis_test/.gitignore. ===
data/*.ifc
data/*.rvt

# The one exception: the example model (9.5 MB), which the
# verify_* scripts and the browser tests run on and whose shard is tracked.
# Keep it byte-identical: its content key names that shard
# (.gitattributes keeps *.ifc out of line-ending normalisation).
!data/example_autcon.ifc

# === Reference-only external clone (NOT src/tempo/, which is this project's
# own deferred GA code and IS tracked - this is a full copy of the separate
# upstream NepomukWolf/vscode-ifc-dev project, kept around only as porting
# reference for Interfaces/Frontend/core/engine/ (see engine/README.md for
# the MIT attribution). 84 files / 5.5MB, including its own package-lock.json,
# CI workflows, docs site, and two .ifc fixture files - nothing outside this
# directory references it, so none of it needs to live in this repo's
# history. Anchored to repo root (leading /) so it does NOT match
# src/tempo/. ===
/tempo/

# Derived frontend artefacts: web-ifc engine files copied
# from node_modules on every dev start/build, and e2e harness output.
Interfaces/Frontend/core/public/wasm/
Interfaces/Frontend/core/scripts/e2e/out/

# Neufert source plans and validation pack (local working copies, not part of the repo history).
/neufert_logic.md
/neufert_ifc_requirement_logic.md
/neufert_validation_pack.json

# === Maintainer notes (local working copies, untracked 2026-10-23): the long
# engineering log and plans (DEV, DETECTORS, PLAN), MODALITY, SIG, RL. The
# public documentation is README.md, CONTRIBUTING.md and docs/. ===
/notes/
# Design studies (local working copies).
/docs/superpowers/
